Level 3 — Multiple Requirements
Q11 Find the 3 highest-paid employees who are older than 25.
Return their:
Name
Age
Salary

Q12 For employees earning more than 40,000, calculate the average salary for each city and display the cities from the highest average salary to the lowest.
Q13 For every employee, calculate what their salary would be after receiving a 10,000 salary increase.
Return:
Name
Current salary
New salary

Q14 Classify every employee according to their salary:
70,000 or more → "High"
Below 70,000 → "Normal"
Return the employee's name, salary, and classification.

Q15 Some employees have a bonus and some don't.
Create a result where every employee has a finalBonus value:
If they have a bonus, use that bonus.
If they don't have a bonus, use 0.
Return the employee's name and finalBonus.

Solutions:
db.employees.aggregate([{$match:{age:{$gt:25}}},{$sort:{salary:-1}},{$limit:3},{$project:{name:1,age:1,salary:1,_id:0}}])
db.employees.aggregate([{$match:{salary:{$gt:40000}}},{$group:{_id:"$address.city",avgEmployees:{$avg:"$salary"}}},{$sort:{avgEmployees:-1}}])
db.employees.aggregate([{$addFields:{incrementedSalary:{$add:["$salary",10000]}}},{$project:{name:1,salary:1,incrementedSalary:1,_id:0}}])
db.employees.aggregate([{$addFields:{classification:{$cond:[{$gte:["$salary",70000]},"High","Normal"]}}},{$project:{name:1,salary:1,classification:1,_id:0}}])
db.employees.aggregate([{$addFields:{finalBonus:{$ifNull:["$bonus",0]}}},{$project:{name:1,finalBonus:1,_id:0}}])

