Q1
For every city, find the employee with the highest salary. If there is a tie, return all tied employees.

db.employees.aggregate([{$group:{_id:"$address.city",maxSalary:{$max:"$salary"},allEmployees:{$push:"$$ROOT"}}},{$project:{_id:0,city:"$_id",maxSalary:1,allEmployees:{$filter:{input:"$allEmployees",as:"employee",cond:{$eq:["$$employee.salary","$maxSalary"]}}}}}])




Q2 — Projects Per Employee

Assume:

employees._id → projects.employeeId

Create a report showing each employee and the number of projects assigned to them.

Employees with zero projects must also appear.

Return:

employeeName
projectCount

Sort from the employee with the most projects to the least.

db.employees.aggregate([{$lookup:{from:"projects",localField:"_id",foreignField:"employeeId",as:"projectsData"}},{$addFields:{projectCount:{$size:"$projectsData"}}},{$project:{_id:0,employeeName:"$name",projectCount:1}},{$sort:{projectCount:-1}}])

💀 Q3 — Department Salary Comparison

For every department, calculate:

departmentName
employeeCount
averageSalary

Then return only departments where the average salary is greater than 60,000.

Departments with no employees should not appear.
db.employees.aggregate([{$lookup:{from:"departments",localField:"departmentId",foreignField:"_id",as:"departmentsData"}},{$unwind:"$departmentsData"},{$group:{_id:"$departmentsData.name",avgSalary:{$avg:"$salary"},employeeCount:{$sum:1}}},{$match:{avgSalary:{$gt:60000}}},{$project:{departmentName:"$_id",_id:0,employeeCount:1,avgSalary:1}}])

☠️ Q4 — Final Boss

Create a management report for employees.

Only consider employees who:

are older than 25
earn at least 40,000

For every city, calculate:

number of employees
average salary
highest salary
lowest salary
total salary

Then determine the highest-paid employee in each city.

Finally, return only the top 3 cities based on average salary.

The final result should contain information equivalent to:

city
employeeCount
averageSalary
highestSalary
lowestSalary
totalSalary
highestPaidEmployee
highestPaidEmployeeSalary

If multiple employees are tied for the highest salary in a city, keep all tied employees.

db.employees.aggregate([{$match:{age:{$gt:25},salary:{$gte:40000}}},{$group:{_id:"$address.city",avgSalary:{$avg:"$salary"},totalEmployees:{$sum:1},highestSalary:{$max:"$salary"},lowestSalary:{$min:"$salary"},totalSalary:{$sum:"$salary"},allEmployees:{$push:"$$ROOT"}}},{$sort:{avgSalary:-1}},{$limit:3},{$addFields:{highestPaidEmployees:{$filter:{input:"$allEmployees",as:"employee",cond:{$eq:["$$employee.salary","$highestSalary"]}}}}},{$project:{city:"$_id",totalEmployees:1,totalSalary:1,lowestSalary:1,highestSalary:1,highestPaidEmployeeSalary:"$highestSalary",highestPaidEmployees:1,avgSalary:1}}])


Q5
For every city, calculate the average of salary + bonus, treating missing bonus as 0.
db.employees.aggregate([
  {
    $group: {
      _id: "$address.city",
      averageTotalCompensation: {
        $avg: {
          $add: [
            "$salary",
            { $ifNull: ["$bonus", 0] }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    $sort: {
      averageTotalCompensation: -1
    }
  },
  {
    $project: {
      _id: 0,
      city: "$_id",
      averageTotalCompensation: 1
    }
  }
])

